I often polypile for silver daggers, and it's pretty much as you
describe. You gather up thousands of unwanted stackable weapons
(arrows, bolts, darts), bless them, then lay them out in groups of
about 4 or 5 to be zapped. A stack of 4 blessed arrows might turn into
4 blessed shiruken, but it's more likely to shudder down to a single
blessed two-handed sword or something. This makes it a very slow
process if you're hoping to get something relatively rare (like silver
daggers of shiruken.)
Eventually you'll get lucky though. Probably won't have to shudder
more than a few thousand items to get a couple dozen ninja stars.

This process is in some ways actually easier in [s]lashem, since
polied items eventually revert (unless you intervene with one of the
appropriate potions), allowing you to re-stack them and try again
later on.



